1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,600
A visual inspector can read a specification and still need a quality

2
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:09,201
engineer’s judgment. SpecLens turns that review into a standard the next inspection

3
00:00:09,201 --> 00:00:13,802
can recall. This is the live application, using real Meta vision and

4
00:00:13,802 --> 00:00:18,020
Hindsight memory. The sample photos are generated, with controlled ink overlays.

5
00:00:18,922 --> 00:00:23,314
First, I choose the white marking sample and turn quality memory off.

6
00:00:23,314 --> 00:00:27,706
The vision model sees the photo and the base specification, without a

7
00:00:27,706 --> 00:00:32,099
learned correction. We keep its actual verdict and explanation rather than forcing

8
00:00:32,099 --> 00:00:33,197
a particular answer.

9
00:00:34,923 --> 00:00:39,159
The live model rejected the part. It already identified a defect, so

10
00:00:39,159 --> 00:00:43,396
this is not a manufactured failure. Its original explanation remains on this

11
00:00:43,396 --> 00:00:45,515
ticket and in the audit record.

12
00:00:46,924 --> 00:00:51,620
The quality engineer records the human standard: sharp white printed characters are

13
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:56,315
ink, while broad natural highlights alone remain acceptable. I explicitly choose reject

14
00:00:56,315 --> 00:01:01,010
and the print class, then save the correction. SpecLens keeps the original

15
00:01:01,010 --> 00:01:05,705
model reasoning beside this human decision and sends the correction to Hindsight.

16
00:01:11,926 --> 00:01:16,866
Now I select another marking, from a different source photo, and enable

17
00:01:16,866 --> 00:01:21,806
quality memory. The base specification stays the same. Hindsight retrieves relevant standards

18
00:01:21,806 --> 00:01:24,688
before the model inspects this new part.

19
00:01:27,928 --> 00:01:32,320
On the second photo, the live model rejected the part. This inspection

20
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:36,711
cites the exact human correction saved a moment ago. Hindsight supplied the

21
00:01:36,711 --> 00:01:41,102
standard, and the base specification stayed fixed. A cited memory is an

22
00:01:41,102 --> 00:01:45,128
observed retrieval step even when the model reaches the same verdict.

23
00:01:46,041 --> 00:01:50,444
The comparison runs this second part twice, once without memory and once

24
00:01:50,444 --> 00:01:54,846
with it. Both arms use the same image, model, and base specification.

25
00:01:54,846 --> 00:01:59,248
I leave the expected decision unlabeled so the screen does not imply

26
00:01:59,248 --> 00:02:00,349
a measured score.

27
00:02:02,049 --> 00:02:06,541
Without memory, the model rejected the part. With memory, it rejected the

28
00:02:06,541 --> 00:02:11,033
part. Both arms reached the same verdict in this run. This is

29
00:02:11,033 --> 00:02:15,525
one paired observation, not a general accuracy claim. The memory-enabled arm records

30
00:02:15,525 --> 00:02:17,022
the correction it used.

31
00:02:18,050 --> 00:02:23,647
Quality memory shows the saved rule, reviewer, original inspection reasoning, and confirmed

32
00:02:23,647 --> 00:02:29,243
sync state. Summarize standards asks Hindsight to reflect over this workspace’s corrections.

33
00:02:29,243 --> 00:02:34,373
The summary supports review; the source correction remains the traceable record.

34
00:02:36,050 --> 00:02:41,067
History keeps all four inspection records, including the two comparison arms. I

35
00:02:41,067 --> 00:02:46,084
can search by reviewer and export the complete workspace as JSON. After

36
00:02:46,084 --> 00:02:51,101
a reload, the original decision, human correction, and saved comparison are still

37
00:02:51,101 --> 00:02:51,519
here.

38
00:02:55,054 --> 00:03:00,760
Workspace settings make the context explicit. The factory, part family, and exact

39
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:06,466
specification revision define a separate memory bank. Changing the specification starts a

40
00:03:06,466 --> 00:03:12,172
new scope. Credentials stay on the server; people remain responsible for disposition.

41
00:03:13,074 --> 00:03:17,458
The useful part is the traceable correction: what the model said, what

42
00:03:17,458 --> 00:03:21,842
the engineer recorded, and which later inspection used that standard. Explore SpecLens

43
00:03:21,842 --> 00:03:26,226
at the public app, or review the source and verification material on

44
00:03:26,226 --> 00:03:26,592
GitHub.
